# Teaching App React Rules

## Stack
- Vite + React + TypeScript + react-router-dom + framer-motion in `frontend/`
- Keep university PPT look in `frontend/src/index.css` (blue header, white slides)

## Routing
- Slides are URL-driven: `/chapter/:chapterId/:slideId`
- Do not reintroduce local index state that fights the router
- Sidebar links to first slide of chapter/section

## Components
- `SlideView` renders bullets, keywords, notes, and `slide.image`
- Prefer extending data over inventing new layout systems
- No code comments in TS/TSX

## When adding chapters
1. Create `frontend/src/data/chapters/ch-{part}-{slug}.ts` (Part A→`ch-a-...`, no numeric prefixes)
2. Export/register in `frontend/src/data/chapters/index.ts`
3. Add chapter id to the right group in `frontend/src/data/parts.ts`
4. Put `image` / `imageAlt` on every new slide; slide ids start with the file stem
5. From `frontend/`: run `npm run check:course` then `npm run build`
